WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.820
So Ra No Wo To

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.180
Why can I not play it right?

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.690
Seriously...

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.880
Noël-chan?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:39.780
Rainy Season Sky
- Quartz Rainbow

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.670
Got your wallet?

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.450
Yes!

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:43.360
ID tag?

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:43.990
Yes!

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:44.700
Handkerchief?

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.330
Yes!

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:45.990
Tissues?

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:46.390
Yes!

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.240
Map?

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:47.910
Yes!

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:48.510
Compass?

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.240
Yes!

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.310
MREs?

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:50.730
Yes!

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.730
Helmet?

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:52.480
Yes!

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.480
Handgun.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.070
Hand grenades.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.240
She's kidding, Kana-chan!

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.530
You scared me for a second...

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.290
After a moment's thought, you
should have caught on.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.080
That's mean, Rio-sempai.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:14.590
Lately, you two really have
been getting along.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.000
Rio's acting like an overprotective mother.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.890
Here's the list for today, OK?

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:29.780
Listen up! Your mission is to go into town
and purchase the supplies on that list.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:30.520
Understood?

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.100
Yes!

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.560
All right, drive safely.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.900
Moving out.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.530
Come back soon!

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.040
We're having pot-au-feu for dinner!

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.020
Come straight home!

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.020
She's like a mom.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:59.900
This is the first time we've gone into
town like this. Right, Noël-chan?

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:00.750
Yes.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:06.010
But this is pretty much my
first time going into town...

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.300
Wow!

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.240
What is that?

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.650
It isn't at all like it was
during the festival.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.300
It's so calm and quiet.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.100
Ow-ow-ow-ow...

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.800
The first was a Nue,
a roof ornament only found in Trois.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.360
It's used to ward off evil spirits.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.240
The other was a drinking fountain,

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:48.480
modeled after the twelfth
Helvetian Archduke, Akira Arkadia II.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:53.890
We're here.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.200
You meant what we just saw?

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:57.780
Yes.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.750
I was told to drive safely.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.550
Thanks!

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:02.760
That's really impressive.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.400
Noël-chan, you're really smart!

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.870
Girls?

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.730
You coming or going?
Make up your mind.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.960
You're blocking the store.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.020
The old lady from the festival!

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.840
The lady, you mean.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.800
Pressuring people is wrong.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.600
That's not very nice of you.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.930
How about "Naomi," at least?

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.350
Naomi-san...

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.400
So, the next shipment's
next month?

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.250
Yes.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.850
By the way, does she know?

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.350
No.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.460
You are some weird girls...

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.060
Not like any soldiers I've se-

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:04.670
Um...

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.040
Wh-What?

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.590
About that?

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.950
You were staring at it the first
time you were here, too.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.270
You like it?

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.100
Um... C-Can I touch it?

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:35.460
A-flat.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:42.540
This is a fish, right?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.480
What's it called?

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.330
That's...

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:47.260
It's not a fish.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:49.100
Huh? But...

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:50.150
It's a dolphin.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:53.610
It's more like a human than a fish.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:57.040
It was a marine mammal,
back when life still existed in the sea.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:57.950
The sea?

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.150
It lived in the sea?

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:02.980
Wow...

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:10.700
The old guy's pretty good
at making those.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.410
He may not look it, but
he's a romantic.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.930
Do you know the person
who made it?

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.700
There's a big factory
outside town.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.560
All our glasswork
come from there.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:27.000
I'd love to see them being made.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:27.960
It's OK.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:28.710
What is?

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.200
We're going there right now.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:40.710
I see. You're having them make
parts for the Takemikazuchi.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:45.190
Yes. Naomi is getting parts
from the old era, too.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:49.870
But you're really amazing, Noël-chan.

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.870
You can fix a complicated
machine just like that!

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.020
Just like that?

00:07:54.700 --> 00:08:00.810
I have a really hard time memorizing
the codes for the signal trumpet.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.710
It's really not that hard...

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.710
Machines don't betray you.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.150
Noël-chan-

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:15.890
Your change is 2,750,000 yen!

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:18.710
We get that much back?

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.370
We don't.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.510
It's 2 yen 75 sen.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.960
You're the same as
always, Noël-chan.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:27.900
Here you go.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:29.900
She's right.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.850
That morning trumpet...
Is that you?

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:34.550
Y-Yes.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:37.010
I'm sorry I'm not very good yet...

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.100
It's fine. I like it!

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:43.160
It... Well, it really wakes you up!

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.070
Stare...

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:56.190
I was thinking I need to improve so
I won't bother the townspeople.

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:06.690
Seiya, that's not fair!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.020
Kanata, I-

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.480
Come get it then!

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:13.160
Ow...

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:14.240
Sorr-

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.270
You hit someone!

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.020
I'm so sorry!

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.910
You're...

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:25.800
The girl from the festival!

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:25.800
The clumsy girl!

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:31.800
I'm glad that you seem
to be better.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.810
You murderer!

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:51.320
Seiya-san, these people have nothing
to do with your parents!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.690
They're all the same!

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.400
I hate soldiers!

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:56.290
Get out of our town!

00:09:56.290 --> 00:10:00.720
Playing your crap trumpet every morning...
<i>It's annoying!</i>

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.950
Hey, Seiya!

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:07.890
I'm really sorry for his rudeness.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:09.100
I-It's OK.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.980
He's a war orphan.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:15.000
So he gets really angry whenever
he sees a soldier.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.030
Noël-chan.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:19.430
It's OK.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:23.150
He's right. We're soldiers.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:25.430
So...

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:27.550
Noël-chan...

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:05.760
He's right. We're soldiers.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:10.160
When I enlisted, I repeated
the Oath of Paradores.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.490
So I thought I understood that...

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:16.280
What am I saying?

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.590
I always understood it.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.900
I won't start whining now!

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.410
That's right.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:28.540
I have to get better in case
something happens.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.950
Everyone would be in trouble if there
wasn't a signal trumpet.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:32.890
We're almost there.

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:38.680
That's the glass factory?

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.330
Wow, Noël-chan!

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:44.510
I've never seen a building
that big!

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.530
This one's no good, either.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:08.200
Is the problem with
optical aberration?

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:11.110
I'm sure I've got the
right refraction.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.810
I-I'm the new recruit,
Kanata Sorami!

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:23.390
Nice to meet you all!

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:27.490
Uh, I...

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:31.140
So, how was it until
it put up the error?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.330
The seek time was
essentially the same.

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:37.650
The distortion along the peripheral
area was less than last time...

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:37.650
Sorry!

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:43.440
The boss gets really focused when
he starts to talk about work.

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:46.660
But you know, he's amazing,
old man Carl.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:53.170
He's one of the five people in the nation
bearing the title of Meister.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:58.170
He won a competition in the capital, and he
once presented his work to the Archduke!

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.170
Maria! If there's time for talk,
there's time for work!

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:06.140
Right! I'm sorry, boss.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:10.380
I'm not worthy of the
title, anyway.

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:13.140
I'm nothing compared to this.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.760
What is it?

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:18.440
The lens to the Takemikazuchi's
optic sensor.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.480
That's the real one.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:26.370
I need two to repair it, so I asked
him to make another.

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:28.680
But it's not going well.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.490
It's so pretty, though.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:34.290
In addition to its primary component
of silicon dioxide,

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:38.450
the lens is infused with sodium
oxide and magnesium oxide.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:41.660
This corrects for the chromatic
and peripheral aberrations.

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:44.600
In other words, for the distortion
in the captured image.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.840
But we don't know how it's distributed
through the lens.

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:53.600
It's a product of the previous
era's magic-like technology.

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:03.110
I thought glass was just pretty,
but it's complex, as well.

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:09.720
Seize has high-quality
silica deposits,

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:13.960
so it's always had a number of small studios
that primarily made works of art.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.760
This was originally one of them.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:24.040
However, as the war intensified, the demand grew
for the glass used in military applications.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:28.380
This factory prospered
because of the war.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:45.330
Kanata, I like machines.

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:46.320
Yes.

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:50.550
But sometimes machines
hurt people.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:55.830
I'm sure in the past, the Takemikazuchi
killed a lot of people.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:04.140
Do you think a machine that killed
a lot of people is scary?

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:07.340
Yes.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:16.350
But I guess I'm more afraid of the people
who used it than the machine itself.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.390
Because this trumpet...

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:25.750
When I play it, it's awful. But when
Rio-sempai plays it, it's so pretty.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.780
I'm sure a tank is the
same kind of thing.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:37.210
And a while ago, Rio-sempai played
me a song from inside it.

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:39.610
It can make such beautiful music!

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:56.310
I'm sure it's a good tank!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.560
I know! Why don't...

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.760
Noël-chan.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:17.490
Let her rest.

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:23.330
I bet she was up all night again.

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:28.400
Noël-chan's working really hard
at fixing the Takemikazuchi.

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:29.510
I know.

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:33.210
She's a real craftsman.

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:38.060
If she weren't, I wouldn't make something
that's as big a pain in the ass as this.

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:42.290
Here, put this on her.

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.090
Thank you.

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:48.550
By the way, you guys stopped
by Windmill right?

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:50.470
How's Naomi-san?

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:52.550
Yes!

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:56.530
She said your boss was
a wonderful romantic.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.230
She said so?

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:00.120
Wonderful. Eh, boss?

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:02.000
Shut up!

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.210
Get to work!

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:06.810
Oh! He's mad!

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.210
Gotta get to work!

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:19.950
But is the technology from
the past that amazing?

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:21.290
It is, yeah.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:25.160
But the boss always says,

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:29.890
"You know, no matter how amazing
it is, humans just like us made it.

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:32.990
So we could make it, too!"

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.160
You agree, don't you?

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:38.240
Yes. Or I'd like to say yes, but...

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.210
I see...

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:50.380
You're right. Rio-san's trumpet playing
is very different from yours.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.910
It's really bothering me.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:55.070
How can I be like her?

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:58.480
I think I'm practicing
as hard as I can!

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:02.300
My lips, you see, they're
so swollen.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.430
But...

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:09.840
I try and try, but it doesn't
sound like hers.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:13.520
I guess I really don't have the talent...

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:14.390
Miss.

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:14.990
Yes!

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:19.350
"Talent" is the worst excuse cited
by people who give up.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:20.900
Give me that.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.950
I don't understand
trumpets, but...

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:30.130
I do know there's a mistake
the young often make.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.960
Miss, are you trying to force
yourself to make the sound?

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:07.730
I'm not trying to make
it this shape.

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:11.790
The glass wants to be this shape.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:22.600
Thank you, Mr. Carl!

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:55.590
Like the sound wants
to play itself...

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:44.470
Morning?

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.180
Yes.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:50.470
It looks like the sun came
up a bit early for her.

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:53.320
She's a craftsman
in her own right.

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:54.480
It's a good sound!

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:57.480
Sound?

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:05.200
The sound glass makes
changes slightly,

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:08.700
depending on the number of
impurities and their type.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:12.080
Even if we can't hear
the difference,

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:15.720
someone with talented
ears could.

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:18.970
I'm going to have you
listen for the sound

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:21.790
that's closest to it from the
samples we've made so far.

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:23.770
That will probably...

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:28.220
Now, listen to their voices, miss!

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.510
Yes!

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:52.980
Since she arrived, Noël-chan
has changed a lot.

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:54.110
You think?

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:55.160
Yeah!

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:18.060
You did it!

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.650
You did it, Noël-chan!

00:22:24.580 --> 00:22:26.150
Thank you.

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:35.160
I've never seen Noël
smile before.

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:19.980
Mountain Hiking - The Ends of the World

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:17.080
Next time:

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:18.020
Mountain Hiking.

